==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|residu|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|residuum|lang=la}}, neuter of {{term|residuus||remaining|lang=la}}, from {{term|resideō||I remain behind|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Whatever [[remain]]s after something else has been [[removed]].
# {{context|chemistry|lang=en}} The [[substance]] that remains after [[evaporation]], [[distillation]], [[filtration]] or any similar process.
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} Whatever [[property]] or [[effect]]s are left in an [[estate]] after payment of all debts, other charges and deduction of what is specifically [[bequeathed]] by the [[testator]].
# {{context|mathematics|lang=en}} A form of [[complex number]], [[proportional]] to the [[contour integral]] of a [[meromorphic]] [[function]] along a [[path]] enclosing one of its [[singularity|singularities]].

